  "summary": [
    "Anchor from the reference class: IOM Missing Migrants Project Central Mediterranean deaths; February 2026 count around 606 informs a base-rate starting point.",
    "February pace suggests March could for a while reach or exceed 900 deaths by end-March, given historical variability and early-2026 dynamics.",
    "Key upward updates: continuation of the February pace, gear-shifting weather/sea conditions increasing fatalities, and constrained rescue capacity raising mortality risk.",
    "Downward and mitigating factors: potential policy tightening reducing crossings and reporting lags could dampen near-term tallies, contributing to calibration uncertainty."
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "narrative": "Starting from the Mediterranean Central Mediterranean reference class with February 2026 counts (~606) as the anchor, March remains plausibly capable of reaching 900 deaths if the pace continues and weather/SAR pressures persist. Downside risks from policy reductions and reporting lags temper the forecast, yielding a calibrated 77% posterior with notable uncertainty around near-term revisions.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.25,
      "basis": "Reference class anchored on IOM Central Mediterranean fatalities; February 2026 total ~606 provides a low base-rate starting point for a short-horizon (end-March) forecast."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "March pace continuation from February 2026",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "606 deaths through February implies March would need roughly 294 more deaths to hit 900; if March maintains or exceeds February’s pace, the target remains plausible."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Adverse weather and rough seas increasing fatalities",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Early 2026 storm activity/SAR risk can elevate fatalities, lifting the March total beyond a flat pace scenario."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Reduction in NGO search-and-rescue capacity due to policy crackdowns",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Diminished rescue assets raise mortality risk on crossings, pushing the March tally higher than in a more permissive SAR environment."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Expansion of SAR capacity and safe-migration pathways",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "If SAR capacity or safer routes improve, mortality could be contained, lowering the March total relative to a severe-pace scenario."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Reporting lag and inherent near-term volatility in IOM counts",
        "direction": "neutral",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Timeliness and revisions in near-term counts introduce uncertainty; March tallies may be revised up or down after initial releases."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "We begin with a base-rate anchor around February's 606 deaths, then apply modest-to-strong upward shifts for March pace, weather events, and SAR constraints, while incorporating downward pressure from policy tightening and a weak neutral factor for reporting volatility. The combination yields a calibrated posterior around 0.77, with a range capturing substantial near-term uncertainty due to data revisions and episodic events."
  }
}

